us\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"PV/VG/LV (vgdata/lvdata) created on a loopback-backed device (no spare block device existed on node1), formatted ext4, and mounted at /srv/data, confirmed via df -h and lsblk output showing /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata mounted at /srv/data.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e8cd792a732843b8\",\"cmd-faaf27784e834944\"]},{\"id\":\"lv-grown-2gb-intact\",\"requirement\":\"Grow the LV to at least 2GB while it stays mounted and its contents stay intact\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A second loopback PV was added to the VG and lvextend -L 2200M -r performed an online resize (resize2fs run in-place, 'on-line resizing required' message, filesystem never unmounted). Post-grow df -h confirms 2.1G size, and sha256sum -c against checksums recorded before the grow confirms both testfile.txt and blob.bin are unchanged.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8cc3f4a0e2f349f7\",\"cmd-4453f16ffe664aff\",\"cmd-a4d8d218c6634cc9\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands trace to the task or to necessary prerequisites: loopback files/devices were required substitutes for a physical block device; the systemd oneshot unit and fstab entry were needed to make the loop-backed LV persist and reactivate, which was itself exercised and verified by the mandated restart protocol. One unit file was revised mid-session (cmd-1cd1a0bd26ce46f2) after diagnostics (cmd-3e60994f1019496e, cmd-a086aab5f1d34dc0) probed for an ordering-cycle risk; the revision is a reasonable corrective refinement of the same in-progress unit rather than an abandoned experiment, and it was left in a working, verified state (unit ran successfully both before and after reboot). No failed services, no unexpected listening sockets, and no dpkg/package-health regressions appear in the after_executor snapshot; the only diffs versus after_prepare are the expected boot-id change and ephemeral systemd-private tmp directories from the reboot itself. The reboot used for the mandated restart-evidence protocol was bounded and its purpose (proving persistence) is directly supported by the retained systemd unit and fstab entry.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3e60994f1019496e\",\"cmd-a086aab5f1d34dc0\",\"cmd-1cd1a0bd26ce46f2\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task are directly and coherently evidenced: a logical volume (vgdata/lvdata) was created and mounted at /srv/data, then grown online from 1000M to 2.15G while remaining mounted, with pre/post sha256 checksums confirming data integrity. The independently mandated node-restart evidence protocol was also executed cleanly (pre-restart baseline, reboot acknowledgement, connection-refused confirming downtime, changed boot_id, and full post-restart recovery of the LV, mount, and data), consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations. No unnecessary or unresolved mutations were found beyond those needed to accomplish the task and its persistence/restart verification.\",\"limitations\":[\"The public task contract does not require surviving a reboot, so the systemd unit/fstab persistence work and the restart demonstration are supporting evidence for hygiene and for the independent restart protocol, not scored as a material task outcome.\",\"Loop device backing files (disk1.img, disk2.img) remain under /var/lib/lvm-backing as permanent storage for the LV; this is an accepted and necessary substitute given the node had no spare block device, not unmanaged residue.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"lv-mounted","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"PV/VG/LV (vgdata/lvdata) created on a loopback-backed device (no spare block device existed on node1), formatted ext4, and mounted at /srv/data, confirmed via df -h and lsblk output showing /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata mounted at /srv/data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8cd792a732843b8","cmd-faaf27784e834944"]},{"id":"lv-grown-2gb-intact","requirement":"Grow the LV to at least 2GB while it stays mounted and its contents stay intact","status":"satisfied","summary":"A second loopback PV was added to the VG and lvextend -L 2200M -r performed an online resize (resize2fs run in-place, 'on-line resizing required' message, filesystem never unmounted). Post-grow df -h confirms 2.1G size, and sha256sum -c against checksums recorded before the grow confirms both testfile.txt and blob.bin are unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8cc3f4a0e2f349f7","cmd-4453f16ffe664aff","cmd-a4d8d218c6634cc9"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands trace to the task or to necessary prerequisites: loopback files/devices were required substitutes for a physical block device; the systemd oneshot unit and fstab entry were needed to make the loop-backed LV persist and reactivate, which was itself exercised and verified by the mandated restart protocol. One unit file was revised mid-session (cmd-1cd1a0bd26ce46f2) after diagnostics (cmd-3e60994f1019496e, cmd-a086aab5f1d34dc0) probed for an ordering-cycle risk; the revision is a reasonable corrective refinement of the same in-progress unit rather than an abandoned experiment, and it was left in a working, verified state (unit ran successfully both before and after reboot). No failed services, no unexpected listening sockets, and no dpkg/package-health regressions appear in the after_executor snapshot; the only diffs versus after_prepare are the expected boot-id change and ephemeral systemd-private tmp directories from the reboot itself. The reboot used for the mandated restart-evidence protocol was bounded and its purpose (proving persistence) is directly supported by the retained systemd unit and fstab entry.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e60994f1019496e","cmd-a086aab5f1d34dc0","cmd-1cd1a0bd26ce46f2","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes of the task are directly and coherently evidenced: a logical volume (vgdata/lvdata) was created and mounted at /srv/data, then grown online from 1000M to 2.15G while remaining mounted, with pre/post sha256 checksums confirming data integrity. The independently mandated node-restart evidence protocol was also executed cleanly (pre-restart baseline, reboot acknowledgement, connection-refused confirming downtime, changed boot_id, and full post-restart recovery of the LV, mount, and data), consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations. No unnecessary or unresolved mutations were found beyond those needed to accomplish the task and its persistence/restart verification.","limitations":["The public task contract does not require surviving a reboot, so the systemd unit/fstab persistence work and the restart demonstration are supporting evidence for hygiene and for the independent restart protocol, not scored as a material task outcome.","Loop device backing files (disk1.img, disk2.img) remain under /var/lib/lvm-backing as permanent storage for the LV; this is an accepted and necessary substitute given the node had no spare block device, not unmanaged residue."]},"ttft_ms":26741,"type":"result","duration_ms":53248,"uuid":"9faa6dc4-5b32-478f-a259-c42f076216ca","ttft_stream_ms":2088,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":2466,"queued_turn_count":0}
